<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Apply on KevCaz's Website</title><link>https://kevcaz.github.io/tags/apply/</link><description>Recent content in Apply on KevCaz's Website</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><copyright>Content under CC0 1.0 Universal unless otherwise specified.</copyright><lastBuildDate>Wed, 01 Jul 2020 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://kevcaz.github.io/tags/apply/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Beware of `apply()` outputs!</title><link>https://kevcaz.github.io/notes/2020/07/2020-07-01_beware_of_apply/</link><pubDate>Wed, 01 Jul 2020 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://kevcaz.github.io/notes/2020/07/2020-07-01_beware_of_apply/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;I have been frequently using &lt;a href="https://www.datacamp.com/community/tutorials/r-tutorial-apply-family"&gt;&lt;code&gt;apply()&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; for years now, quite happily. But yesterday, I was surprised by how &lt;code&gt;apply()&lt;/code&gt; works and in this note I&amp;rsquo;ll try to explaining why.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Let&amp;rsquo;s consider the following data frame.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div style="color:#575279;background-color:#faf4ed;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;"&gt;
&lt;table style="border-spacing:0;padding:0;margin:0;border:0;"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="vertical-align:top;padding:0;margin:0;border:0;"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#575279;background-color:#faf4ed;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span style="white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#7f7f7f"&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="vertical-align:top;padding:0;margin:0;border:0;;width:100%"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#575279;background-color:#faf4ed;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-R" data-lang="R"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;R&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#797593"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;df0&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#797593"&gt;&amp;lt;-&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;data.frame&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#797593"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;v1&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#797593"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#286983"&gt;letters&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;[1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#797593"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#ea9d34"&gt;3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#797593"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;v2&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#797593"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#ea9d34"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#797593"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#ea9d34"&gt;3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#797593"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;And let&amp;rsquo;s assume I need to convert all columns, irrespective of their class, to
columns of character strings (this example is somewhat contrived, but
illustrates well the issue). As passing &lt;code&gt;df0&lt;/code&gt; to &lt;code&gt;as.character()&lt;/code&gt; is clearly not
the solution:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>